# Secrets — NEVER commit. See .env.example for the billing-trap warning.
# Ignore EVERY .env variant (.env, .env.local, .env.<anything>) and re-include
# only the checked-in placeholder. The test-data-seed skill READS a live admin
# bearer token (QA_ADMIN_TOKEN) from .env — the ONLY env file anything loads
# (playwright.config.ts's bare dotenv.config() and the CLAUDE.md shell loader
# both read .env alone; a token parked in .env.test would never be loaded). The
# HUMAN puts it there (.claude/settings.json does NOT grant agents Write/Edit on
# .env — it's outside the write-allowlist, so an agent write needs explicit
# per-prompt human approval; an agent needing a new var asks the human or uses an
# explicitly approved Bash append). A bare `.env`/`.env.*.local`
# list would leave variant files committable (F-001). The `!.env.example`
# negation keeps the template tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Playwright + QA runtime artifacts (regenerated every run) — with ONE carve-out:
# artifacts/route-manifests/ is DURABLE per-/qa-warden:gen data, not per-run output. It is
# the sole input to /qa-warden:impact and /qa-warden:coverage's flow footprint (no grep fallback),
# so it must survive a fresh clone/CI checkout — commit manifests with the spec/test
# they belong to. `artifacts/*` (not `artifacts/`) because git cannot re-include a
# path inside an excluded DIRECTORY; the negation below needs the wildcard form.
artifacts/*
!artifacts/route-manifests/
test-results/
playwright-report/
playwright/.cache/
blob-report/
all-blob-reports/
# playwright-cli session byproducts (DOM/AX snapshots + console logs) — never commit;
# they can contain page content and are regenerated on every CLI drive. `.playwright/`
# is the sibling scratch dir the CLI/MCP self-test leaves behind (RUN-20) — same deal.
.playwright-cli/
.playwright/
# Microsoft's official @playwright/cli skill, installed into .claude/skills/ by
# /qa-warden:init every run (`npx playwright-cli install --skills`) — regenerated, not source,
# and it churns on each re-init. The plugin ships its OWN thin companion skill
# separately; don't commit the vendored official copy (F-006). `git add -f` if a team
# deliberately wants it pinned for offline use.
.claude/skills/playwright-cli/
# Suite run output — regenerated every run, never source. Covers the /qa-warden:report
# summary, /qa-warden:run mode=single per-command JSON, and /qa-warden:review url= findings so none of them
# land as tracked VCS churn. If you WANT to keep a specific audit report, `git add -f`.
reports/summary.md
reports/headless-*.json
reports/headless-*.log
reports/audit-*.md
reports/coverage-*.md
# Wave-2 output of scripts/README.md's nightly recipe (`--reporter=json > reports/regression.json`)
reports/regression.json

# NOTE: bug reports under bugs/ ARE tracked source. The healer and CLAUDE.md
# §"Bug-report schema" write triaged defects to bugs/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>.md and link
# them from `test.fixme(...)`, so they are the durable defect record, not throwaway
# drafts — do NOT gitignore them. (A former `bugs/auto/` ignore rule was dead: no agent
# ever wrote there, and ignoring it contradicted the tracked-bugs model.)

# Playwright storageState — auth cookies. NEVER commit.
# The seed writes per-site files: fixtures/auth.app.json, fixtures/auth.admin.json
fixtures/auth*.json

# `/qa-warden:init --resync` backups. The resync force-refreshes toolkit-owned substrate
# (package.json, playwright.config.ts, prod-guard.*, …) and backs up each changed file
# to <file>.qa-bak first. They are transient — review, then delete — so they must never
# be committed: a stray `playwright.config.ts.qa-bak` is a confusing near-duplicate of
# the live substrate that later readers mistake for a real config.
*.qa-bak

